% The Ponens policies misra-cpp, as a program of Logical English for LPS.
%
% Written by lpsPlus's ponens_twin.pl (docs/migration/ponens.md) from 12
% Ponens policies, whose files are in sources/ (Ponens: github.com/imandra-ai/
% ponens, MIT licence, Imandra Inc.), with 2 Ponens traces as its scenarios.
%
% Each step of a trace is an action of the session Ponens recorded. Each
% policy is a causal law that records a breach: at the step where the policy
% fails, when the step ends, or at the end of the session when the policy
% looks forward. Where a scenario has a comment above it, the comment is what
% Ponens's own evaluator (`ponens trace check --json`) says of the same
% policies on that trace.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from the policies of
% another system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
% express or implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or
% fit for a particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against
% its source before relying on it. It is not legal, regulatory or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 22.

the events are:
    step *a step* is a *a kind*; known as step_is_a.
    step *a step* shows *a sign*; known as step_shows.
    step *a step* ends; known as step_ends.
    the trace shows *a sign*; known as trace_shows.
    the session ends; known as session_ends.

the fluents are:
    step *a step* was a *a kind*; known as was_a.
    step *a step* has shown *a sign*; known as has_shown.
    step *a step* has ended; known as has_ended.
    the trace has shown *a sign*; known as trace_has_shown.
    step *a step* meets *a condition*; known as meets.
    the trace meets *a condition*; known as trace_meets.
    the policy *a policy* is broken at step *a step*; known as broken_at.
    the policy *a policy* is broken; known as broken.

the knowledge base misra cpp includes:

% What a trace records, kept to the end of the session.
when step a step is a a kind
then step the step was a the kind.

when step a step shows a sign
then step the step has shown the sign.

when step a step ends
then step the step has ended.

when the trace shows a sign
then the trace has shown the sign.

% misra_cpp_advisory_violation_recorded (warning): G(advisory_violation → recorded)
% MISRA Compliance:2020: Advisory guidelines are best practice; departures need not be formal deviations but should be recorded.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "advisory violation"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "recorded"
then the policy misra_cpp_advisory_violation_recorded is broken at step the step.

% misra_cpp_compliance_summary_produced (error): F(ComplianceSummary)
% MISRA Compliance:2020: the GCS is the primary record of compliance, with an entry for every guideline, its compliance level, deviations and re-categorizations.
the trace meets "some step is a ComplianceSummary" at a time if
    step a step has ended at the time
    and step the step was a ComplianceSummary at the time.

when the session ends
    and it is not the case that the trace meets "some step is a ComplianceSummary"
then the policy misra_cpp_compliance_summary_produced is broken.

% misra_cpp_deviation_documented (error): G(Deviation → rationale_recorded ∧ deviation_approved)
% MISRA Compliance:2020: a deviation is a documented violation of a guideline with supporting rationale, approved via the formal deviation procedure.
step a step meets "shows rationale recorded and shows deviation approved" at a time if
    step the step has shown "rationale recorded" at the time
    and step the step has shown "deviation approved" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deviation
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows rationale recorded and shows deviation approved"
then the policy misra_cpp_deviation_documented is broken at step the step.

% misra_cpp_directives_addressed (error): G(Directive → addressed_with_evidence)
% MISRA: a Directive's compliance cannot be fully defined by the guideline alone; the project must show evidence it has been addressed.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Directive
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "addressed with evidence"
then the policy misra_cpp_directives_addressed is broken at step the step.

% misra_cpp_enforcement_plan_defined (warning): G(StaticAnalysis → enforcement_plan)
% MISRA Compliance:2020: the GEP records, for every guideline, the analysis tool(s), manual review, or other means used to enforce it.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a StaticAnalysis
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "enforcement plan"
then the policy misra_cpp_enforcement_plan_defined is broken at step the step.

% misra_cpp_mandatory_not_weakened (error): G(recategorization → ¬weakens_mandatory)
% MISRA Compliance:2020: Required and Advisory may be made stricter; Mandatory cannot be loosened, and only Advisory may be re-categorized to Disapplied.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "recategorization"
    and step the step has shown "weakens mandatory"
then the policy misra_cpp_mandatory_not_weakened is broken at step the step.

% misra_cpp_no_mandatory_deviation (error): G(Deviation → ¬targets_mandatory)
% MISRA Compliance:2020: Mandatory guidelines cannot be deviated; a deviation may only target a Required or (re-categorized) Advisory guideline.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deviation
    and step the step has shown "targets mandatory"
then the policy misra_cpp_no_mandatory_deviation is broken at step the step.

% misra_cpp_no_mandatory_violation (error): G(¬mandatory_violation)
% MISRA Compliance:2020: all Mandatory guidelines must be followed to achieve compliance; deviations are not allowed.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "mandatory violation"
then the policy misra_cpp_no_mandatory_violation is broken at step the step.

% misra_cpp_recategorization_in_grp (error): G(recategorization → P(grp_documented))
% MISRA Compliance:2020: the GRP records all agreed category changes for the project before they take effect.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows grp documented" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "grp documented" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "recategorization"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows grp documented"
then the policy misra_cpp_recategorization_in_grp is broken at step the step.

% misra_cpp_required_violation_deviated (error): G(required_violation → P(deviation_approved))
% MISRA Compliance:2020: Required guidelines should be followed, but documented and approved deviations are allowed where justified.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows deviation approved" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "deviation approved" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "required violation"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows deviation approved"
then the policy misra_cpp_required_violation_deviated is broken at step the step.

% misra_cpp_static_analysis_before_commit (error): G(GitCommit → P(StaticAnalysis ∧ misra_cpp_ruleset))
% MISRA Compliance:2020 Guidelines Enforcement Plan (GEP): every guideline has a defined technical enforcement means; analysis must run before code is accepted.
step a step meets "an earlier step is a StaticAnalysis and shows misra cpp ruleset" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a StaticAnalysis at the time
    and step the second step has shown "misra cpp ruleset" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GitCommit
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a StaticAnalysis and shows misra cpp ruleset"
then the policy misra_cpp_static_analysis_before_commit is broken at step the step.

% misra_cpp_undecidable_manually_reviewed (warning): G(undecidable_violation → manual_review)
% MISRA Compliance:2020 / guideline decidability: undecidable rules cannot be fully checked by a tool, so manual review is required to confirm compliance.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "undecidable violation"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "manual review"
then the policy misra_cpp_undecidable_manually_reviewed is broken at step the step.

scenario misra_cpp_governed is:
    % Ponens: every policy of the pack passes on this trace.
    the trace shows "a commit" from 1 to 2.
    step 1 is a StaticAnalysis from 2 to 3.
    step 1 shows "enforcement plan" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 shows "grp documented" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 shows "misra cpp ruleset" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 ends from 3 to 4.
    step 2 shows "recorded" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 is a Deviation from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "rationale recorded" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "deviation approved" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 ends from 5 to 6.
    step 3 is a Directive from 6 to 7.
    step 3 shows "addressed with evidence" from 6 to 7.
    step 3 ends from 7 to 8.
    step 4 shows "required violation" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 ends from 9 to 10.
    step 5 shows "advisory violation" from 10 to 11.
    step 5 shows "recorded" from 10 to 11.
    step 5 ends from 11 to 12.
    step 6 shows "recategorization" from 12 to 13.
    step 6 ends from 13 to 14.
    step 7 shows "undecidable violation" from 14 to 15.
    step 7 shows "manual review" from 14 to 15.
    step 7 ends from 15 to 16.
    step 8 is a GitCommit from 16 to 17.
    step 8 ends from 17 to 18.
    step 9 is a ComplianceSummary from 18 to 19.
    step 9 ends from 19 to 20.
    the session ends from 20 to 21.

scenario misra_cpp_violating is:
    % Ponens (`ponens trace check --json`):
    %     misra_cpp_advisory_violation_recorded: failed at step 3
    %     misra_cpp_compliance_summary_produced: failed
    %     misra_cpp_no_mandatory_violation: failed at step 1
    %     misra_cpp_required_violation_deviated: failed at step 2
    %     misra_cpp_static_analysis_before_commit: failed at step 4
    the trace shows "a commit" from 1 to 2.
    step 1 shows "mandatory violation" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 ends from 3 to 4.
    step 2 shows "required violation" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 ends from 5 to 6.
    step 3 shows "advisory violation" from 6 to 7.
    step 3 ends from 7 to 8.
    step 4 is a GitCommit from 8 to 9.
    step 4 ends from 9 to 10.
    the session ends from 10 to 11.
